From eab7b2eacc67613ec4857c398723ca4ca63a9f9d Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Sun, 18 Oct 2026 19:43:13 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] Standby relay: a second server on a held data dir serves its
 address through serve.sock

Two containers of one app share the data volume during a blue/green
deploy, each with its own loopback. The new container's server waited
on serve.lock and refused connections, so its agent's batches bounced
until the old container exited. With standby_relay (off by default) the
lock holder also listens on <data_dir>/serve.sock, and a standby that
can bind its own address splices every connection to that socket until
it holds the lock, then serves the same listener itself. Connections in
the hand-over gap retry the socket for up to 30 s.

Tests: standby::tests (gap connection, path length) and
tests/standby_relay.rs (45 batches through the standby across a TERM of
the holder, all 200, all stored once); serve_lock still passes.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
